# g95-fu-ssh-service wiring (core)

Written in mixdog-connections / mixdog-ssh / mixdog-app-protocol (src/v2/host_notification.rs). What a hot file or the composition must do:

## 1. mixdog-app-protocol src/v2/mod.rs
Add `pub mod host_notification;` after `pub mod host;`. Rows and type edits: pending-rows/g95-fu-ssh-service.rows.

## 2. The composition of the connections (compose_connections.rs, g9-compose-connections) over the changed seams
- `ConnectionsDeps` has a new field `translate: Arc<dyn Fn(&str) -> String + Send + Sync>`: the English text in, the text in the desktop's UI language out
  (the text itself when there is none). It is used for the pair-code errors of `remoteHosts/redeemCode`. Build it from the language the desktop publishes in
  `hostState.displayPreferences` (`host/state/set` key displayPreferences, `{theme, language}`, sent whenever the link comes up) and the keyed catalogs of
  apps/desktop/src/shared/native-ui-catalogs.json (`include_str!`, one object per language). Add the keys "Too many attempts. Try again in {{seconds}} seconds."
  and "The code is wrong or has expired." to apps/desktop/src/shared/native-ui-keys.json (only "Codes are not available on this connection server yet. Use the QR
  code." is there) and regenerate with apps/desktop/scripts/i18n/native-catalogs.mjs. The notifier's fixed texts (EnglishTexts) can use the same translator.
- `NotifySink` gained `fn close(&self, connection_id: &str)`: HostToasts::close sends
  `host.notify(HostCapability::Notifications, NOTIFICATION_CLOSE, json!({ "connectionId": connection_id }))` with `const NOTIFICATION_CLOSE: Method = Method("host/notification/close")`.
- `NotifySink::show`: a toast carries the PC's sound only when `params.sound.is_some()` (the notifier sets it for a session's final answer and nothing else).
  HostToasts::show: `let style = (self.style)(); if params.sound.is_some() { params.sound = style.sound; params.volume = Some(style.volume); } else { params.sound = None; params.volume = None; }`.
- `NotifyPrefs::view` now returns `Result<PreferencesView, String>` (an unreadable preference is not decided and is offered again): PcPreferences::view returns `Ok(pc_view(&self.0))`
  (pc_view/desktop_settings reading that can fail should map the failure to Err).
- HostWindowFocus::session_on_screen: `window.visible && window.focused && window.session_ids.iter().any(|id| id == session_id)` (WindowFocusEntry.sessionIds, rows file).
- Claim resources: build `let resources = Arc::new(mixdog_ssh::context::ClaimedResources::default())` once. `EnvLoginHelpers::new(ssh_env.clone(), durability_io, user_data_dir, resources.clone())`.
  LocalPayloads::staged opens `StagedPayloads::open(&Unlaned, &resources.applied(&self.env))` (it reads the folder when the first install needs it, after the claim), and the env
  `ServerLogins` and `EnvCleaner` use is `resources.applied(..)` where they read `server_cores_dir`/`askpass_helper`. Drop the composer's own `askpass_helper`/`server_cores_dir` env
  constants: mixdog_ssh::context::{ASKPASS_HELPER_ENV, SERVER_CORES_ENV} are the names. Whoever accepts `host/claim` calls `resources.set(params.resources.clone())` when the claim is
  accepted and `resources.set(None)` when the claimant releases it or goes (the claim handler of the host domain; this is the one line that makes "the desktop sends them" reach the ssh code).
- compose: a failed `MixdogSshConfig::configure` is reported and the service still composes (the desktop's `configured` promise swallowed its failure: ssh then fell back to the user's own files);
  at present ssh_machine returns ComposeError::Remote for it, which takes the whole connections service down. Inspect and connect already wait for the configuration because the
  service is not built before it finishes.

## 3. SERVICE_PENDING (mixdog-app-server-daemon compose_flip.rs)
Nothing: no new service method (host/notification/close is a notification).

## 4. The connections feed
`ConnectionsFeed::source(Some(id))` now also carries `hosts` and `restore`, so a server window's `subscribeSshHostsChanged` fires. No hot-file change.
